{
  "page": 10,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "464",
      "bbox": [
        46.48500061035156,
        33.174598693847656,
        59.1788330078125,
        40.93147277832031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "H. Haj Chhadé et al.",
      "bbox": [
        430.88201904296875,
        33.174598693847656,
        500.029541015625,
        40.93147277832031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Secondly, the binary operations {+, −, ×, /} can be extended to intervals [17]. Let the symbol ⋄refer to any",
      "bbox": [
        57.82500076293945,
        58.51093673706055,
        500.0188903808594,
        68.64289855957031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "binary operation and [x] and [y] denote any two intervals in R, the resulting interval [z] = [x] ⋄[y] is deﬁned as",
      "bbox": [
        46.48553466796875,
        70.95820617675781,
        495.1203308105469,
        81.09016418457031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[z] = [x] ⋄[y] = [{x ⋄y | x ∈[x], y ∈[y]}] .",
      "bbox": [
        46.48651123046875,
        88.02217102050781,
        230.72885131835938,
        98.18104553222656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(5.4)",
      "bbox": [
        480.92462158203125,
        89.02838897705078,
        500.0289001464844,
        98.15412902832031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "If the binary operation ⋄is continuous, as in the case of the usual arithmetic operations, the set {x ⋄y ∈R|x ∈",
      "bbox": [
        46.487518310546875,
        105.08613586425781,
        500.0388488769531,
        115.21809387207031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[x], y ∈[y]} is an interval. Thus,",
      "bbox": [
        46.48748779296875,
        117.54237365722656,
        178.04034423828125,
        127.67433166503906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[x] ⋄[y] = {x ⋄y ∈R|x ∈[x], y ∈[y]}.",
      "bbox": [
        46.48946762084961,
        134.5973663330078,
        211.4282989501953,
        144.60977172851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The extension to intervals of the usual arithmetic operations {+, −, ×, /} is given next. Recall that [x] = [x, x] and",
      "bbox": [
        46.48948669433594,
        151.6608428955078,
        500.0317077636719,
        161.7932891845703
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[y] = [y, y].",
      "bbox": [
        46.486358642578125,
        164.1168975830078,
        97.25299835205078,
        174.2488555908203
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[x] + [y] =",
      "bbox": [
        46.53141403198242,
        185.48268127441406,
        93.9215087890625,
        195.49508666992188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0007",
      "bbox": [
        96.90530395507812,
        174.4849395751953,
        101.57776641845703,
        184.44754028320312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "x + y, x + y",
      "bbox": [
        101.84675598144531,
        185.48268127441406,
        152.73480224609375,
        195.49520874023438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\b",
      "bbox": [
        153.24288940429688,
        174.4850616455078,
        157.91534423828125,
        184.44766235351562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ",",
      "bbox": [
        159.5791015625,
        185.48280334472656,
        162.87672424316406,
        195.44540405273438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[x] −[y] =",
      "bbox": [
        46.530494689941406,
        207.3975372314453,
        93.92059326171875,
        217.40994262695312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0007",
      "bbox": [
        96.90438842773438,
        196.39979553222656,
        101.57685089111328,
        206.36239624023438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "x −y, x −y",
      "bbox": [
        101.84584045410156,
        207.3975372314453,
        152.7344207763672,
        217.41030883789062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\b",
      "bbox": [
        153.2429962158203,
        196.39979553222656,
        157.9154510498047,
        206.36239624023438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ",",
      "bbox": [
        159.57920837402344,
        207.3975372314453,
        162.8768310546875,
        217.36013793945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[x] × [y] =",
      "bbox": [
        46.48577117919922,
        229.31227111816406,
        93.92070007324219,
        239.32467651367188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0007",
      "bbox": [
        96.90449523925781,
        218.31455993652344,
        101.57695770263672,
        228.27716064453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "min(x y, x y, x y, x y), max(x y, x y, x y, x y)",
      "bbox": [
        101.57595825195312,
        229.31227111816406,
        273.3132019042969,
        239.4448699951172
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\b",
      "bbox": [
        273.31219482421875,
        218.31520080566406,
        277.9846496582031,
        228.27780151367188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ".",
      "bbox": [
        279.6394348144531,
        229.3129119873047,
        282.379150390625,
        239.2755126953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(5.5)",
      "bbox": [
        480.94171142578125,
        230.3191375732422,
        500.0264587402344,
        239.4448699951172
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "If the interval [y] does not include the 0 value, one can also deﬁne",
      "bbox": [
        46.486663818359375,
        248.04161071777344,
        310.03436279296875,
        258.173583984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[x]/[y] = [x] × [1/y, 1/y].",
      "bbox": [
        46.486663818359375,
        265.10552978515625,
        158.17935180664062,
        275.2378845214844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Similarly, elementary functions such as exp, ln, cos and sin, can be simply extended to intervals.",
      "bbox": [
        46.484657287597656,
        283.1760559082031,
        430.2322692871094,
        292.30181884765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Furthermore, all operations on intervals can be extended to boxes.",
      "bbox": [
        57.8250846862793,
        295.6233215332031,
        320.387451171875,
        304.74908447265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inclusion Functions.",
      "bbox": [
        46.484657287597656,
        308.0795593261719,
        128.38697814941406,
        317.08575439453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Consider a function f from Rn to Rm. We are interested in computing the image f([x]) of a box [x] by f. This image",
      "bbox": [
        57.8250846862793,
        316.9171142578125,
        500.0276184082031,
        329.66156005859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is often not a box (see Fig. 6) and its expression might be difﬁcult to obtain. An inclusion function approximates",
      "bbox": [
        46.487213134765625,
        332.9913635253906,
        500.0166931152344,
        342.11712646484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "f([x]). Let [f] denote an interval function from IRn to IRm. By deﬁnition, [f] is said to be an inclusion function for f if",
      "bbox": [
        46.488250732421875,
        341.82012939453125,
        500.0379943847656,
        354.56439208984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "f([x]) ⊆[f]([x]),",
      "bbox": [
        46.48565673828125,
        361.495849609375,
        116.46685791015625,
        371.5082702636719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "∀[x] ∈IRn.",
      "bbox": [
        125.86865997314453,
        360.06036376953125,
        173.39772033691406,
        371.5082702636719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(5.6)",
      "bbox": [
        480.941162109375,
        362.50213623046875,
        500.0259094238281,
        371.6278991699219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inclusion functions may be very pessimistic [16]. An inclusion function [f] is minimal if, for any x, [f]([x]) is the",
      "bbox": [
        46.486114501953125,
        378.5598449707031,
        500.0310974121094,
        388.69183349609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "interval hull of f([x]). The minimal inclusion function for f is unique and will be denoted by [f]∗. Refer to Fig. 6",
      "bbox": [
        46.486114501953125,
        389.3106994628906,
        500.0351867675781,
        401.1480712890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for an example.",
      "bbox": [
        46.486846923828125,
        404.4693908691406,
        108.56878662109375,
        413.59515380859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Amongst the main purposes of interval analysis [17] are: ﬁrstly, ﬁnding an inclusion function [f] such that, for",
      "bbox": [
        57.827274322509766,
        415.9194030761719,
        500.0292053222656,
        426.0513916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "most x, [f]([x]) is close to [f]∗([x]); and secondly, ﬁnding it with a convenient computational time.",
      "bbox": [
        46.488861083984375,
        426.66961669921875,
        439.58331298828125,
        438.50762939453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Constraints Satisfaction Problem and Contraction.",
      "bbox": [
        46.48590087890625,
        441.8283996582031,
        249.13018798828125,
        450.8345947265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Another popular topic in interval analysis are the constraints satisfaction problems (CSPs). Let x be a vector of",
      "bbox": [
        57.82632827758789,
        454.2846374511719,
        500.0322265625,
        463.410400390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "n variables xi ∈R, i ∈{1, . . . , n}, i.e. x = (x1, x2, . . . , xn)T . f = ( f1, f2, . . . , fm)T is a multivalued function",
      "bbox": [
        46.48590087890625,
        463.12213134765625,
        500.0271911621094,
        477.1904296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "such as",
      "bbox": [
        46.486724853515625,
        479.1874084472656,
        75.53267669677734,
        488.31317138671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "f(x) = 0.",
      "bbox": [
        46.486724853515625,
        495.2451171875,
        83.31048583984375,
        505.2575378417969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(5.7)",
      "bbox": [
        480.9437255859375,
        496.2513427734375,
        500.0284729003906,
        505.3771057128906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fig. 6 Inclusion function [10]",
      "bbox": [
        46.48500061035156,
        656.5777587890625,
        150.50074768066406,
        664.3345947265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
